& [DocumentationBoundary] is explicit
  + [official] FileRemoteProtocolInfo maps to FILE_REMOTE_PROTOCOL_INFO when the query succeeds
  + [official] error 87 means a parameter is incorrect
  + [official] volume-GUID final paths are not created for network shares
  + [official] GetVolumeInformationByHandleW is unsupported for SMB 3.0
  + [not_officially_established] error 87 universally means local filesystem
  + [consequence] the program must not reinterpret error 87 as a synthetic protocol-zero structure

& [ContractFinding] is structural
  + [profile_0_2_complete] requires both local volume products and a successful remote-protocol structure
  + [target_behavior] does not supply that conjunction
  + [better_shape] separates local-volume completion from remote-protocol rejection instead of requiring both products in one record
  + [query_strategy] local classification should complete after volume-GUID and volume-information success without calling FileRemoteProtocolInfo
  + [remote_branch] should query FileRemoteProtocolInfo only when local-volume classification cannot complete

